This is the exact way to build a robust, enterprise-grade UI. By joining the USERS table directly in the backend, the React frontend doesn't have to do any heavy lifting, and creating a dedicated scrollable box for a 500-word description ensures the layout never breaks.
Here is the complete implementation to achieve this.
### 1. Backend: Update the SQL Queries (Java)
We will update both of your APIs in VoucherRequestServiceImpl.java to perform a LEFT JOIN on the USERS table. We will concatenate the FIRST_NAME and LAST_NAME, and safely fall back to the ID if the user isn't found.
**Update getWorkflowHistory:**
```java
    @Override
    public List<Map<String, Object>> getWorkflowHistory(String batchId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                w.LAST_ACTION_BY, 
                COALESCE(u.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || u.LAST_NAME, w.LAST_ACTION_BY) AS ACTION_USER_NAME, 
                w.LAST_ACTION, 
                w.LAST_ACTION_AT, 
                w.REMARKS 
            FROM VOUCHER_WORKFLOW w 
            LEFT JOIN USERS u ON w.LAST_ACTION_BY = u.USER_ID
            WHERE w.BATCH_ID_FK = ? 
            ORDER BY w.LAST_ACTION_AT ASC
        """;
        
        return jdbcTemplate.queryForList(sql, batchId);
    }

```
**Update getBatchSummaryDetails:**
This query is expanded to join the USERS table twice (once for the Batch Creator, once for the VID Creator) and extracts the rv.CREATED_AT timestamp.
```java
    @Override
    public Map<String, Object> getBatchSummaryDetails(String batchId) {
        String sql = """
            SELECT 
                vp.VID_FK AS VID,
                vp.CREATED_BY AS BATCH_CREATOR_ID,
                COALESCE(bu.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || bu.LAST_NAME, vp.CREATED_BY) AS BATCH_CREATED_BY_NAME,
                vp.CREATED_AT AS BATCH_CREATED_AT,
                vp.CREATORS_ROLE,
                vp.SCHEDULED_TIME,
                vp.EXECUTED_AT,
                vc.CATEGORY_NAME,
                rv.CREATED_BY AS VID_CREATOR_ID,
                COALESCE(vu.FIRST_NAME || ' ' || vu.LAST_NAME, rv.CREATED_BY) AS VID_CREATED_BY_NAME,
                rv.CREATED_AT AS VID_CREATED_AT,
                rv.DESCRIPTION
            FROM VOUCHER_POSTING vp
            LEFT JOIN REQUEST_VOUCHER rv ON vp.VID_FK = rv.VID
            LEFT JOIN VOUCHER_CATEGORY vc ON rv.CATEGORY_ID = vc.ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS bu ON vp.CREATED_BY = bu.USER_ID
            LEFT JOIN USERS vu ON rv.CREATED_BY = vu.USER_ID
            WHERE vp.BATCH_ID = ?
        """;
        
        try {
            return jdbcTemplate.queryForMap(sql, batchId);
        } catch (EmptyResultDataAccessException e) {
            return new HashMap<>();
        }
    }

```
